
##Loan Eligibility Checker##

Approves a loan only if ALL three conditions are met:
  1. Credit score  >= 700          (boundary: 700 itself IS approved)
  2. Annual income >= 30000        (boundary: 30000 itself IS approved)
  3. Years at job  >= 2            (boundary: 2 itself IS approved)

Pattern used: multiple decision paths joined by boolean AND logic.
All three conditions must independently be true for approval;
failing any single one results in denial.



def check_loan_eligibility():
    credit_score = int(input("Enter credit score: "))
    annual_income = float(input("Enter annual income: "))
    years_at_job = float(input("Enter years at current job: "))

    # Boundary conditions: >= means the boundary value itself qualifies
    # Boolean logic: all three must be True (AND) for approval
    credit_ok = credit_score >= 700
    income_ok = annual_income >= 30000
    job_ok = years_at_job >= 2

    if credit_ok and income_ok and job_ok:
        print("Result: Loan Approved")
    else:
        print("Result: Loan Denied")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    check_loan_eligibility()
